-- NUMERICS: division and modulo signs. Measured: C semantics — quotient
-- truncates toward zero, remainder takes the DIVIDEND's sign. §12 B-4 says
-- "i64/i64 truncates ... % matches", which this satisfies. It diverges from
-- Lua, which floors: Lua answers -4 and 1 for the first pair.
-- expect: -3 -3 -1 1
main = (): i64
    a = -7 / 2
    b = 7 / -2
    c = -7 % 2
    d = 7 % -2
    print("{a} {b} {c} {d}")
    0
end
